// Taxes, rents, tolls and treasuries (taxes spec 2.2, decisions T1-T6; integration notes T7 and on in docs/specs/taxes-and-treasuries.md). Amounts are mites (100 mites = 1 crown).
// Hearth tax per household and season at the four named levels (plan 4A.2): about 2 crowns at Normal, 30 percent of the fief's receipts go on to the realm's treasury.
// A rented dwelling pays by type; a tenant of the lord pays none and owes labour service. Coin parcel rent (320 mites a field and year, autumn), share rents and the 10 percent tithe in kind live in content/base/farming (single source, decision T8).
// Arrears carry over, become a debt after 3 seasons and end in eviction after 6; labour on the demesne works them off at 2 worker-days per 100 mites.
// Unrest rungs: rumours 200, evasion 350, riot 550, revolt brewing 750. Staff wages are mites a day. The lord keeps 40 percent of what the treasury holds above two seasons of payroll.
